    <constant>
        <name>TM_BATCH_SLEEP_BACKOFF</name>
        <uuid>_a-0000ec5e-d78c-8000-9bc5-011c48011c48_11749</uuid>
        <description>Exponential backoff is used to sleep longer and longer each time no transactions are found to start.

Change this value to affect how much additional time is added. A value of 2 doubles each empty sleep cycle (e.g. 20s -&gt; 40s -&gt; 80s, etc). The sleep impact resets back to 0 as soon as a transaction is ready to start.

A value of 1.6s will result in 20s -&gt; 32s -&gt; 51s -&gt; 82s

The maximum sleep time is capped at cons!TM_BATCH_SLEEP_SEC_MAX</description>
        <parentUuid>_a-0000e41e-1753-8000-9ba9-011c48011c48_3274097</parentUuid>
